cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Perigee: plain-language anomaly triage for spacecraft telemetry"
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hrebeniuk
    given-names: Mykyta
  - family-names: Goyal
    given-names: Eklavya
  - family-names: Bhalla
    given-names: Annie
  - alias: Luraxx
repository-code: "https://github.com/eklavyagoyal/ehl-zurich-hackathon-submission"
abstract: >-
  A time-series language model (OpenTSLM SoftPrompt, Llama-3.2-3B, LoRA)
  fine-tuned on ESA Mission1 subsystem_5 telemetry to classify six-hour windows
  as nominal or anomalous and explain the verdict in natural language. Includes a
  reusable TimeNet connector, an agentic dataset-sourcing pipeline, and a
  four-way baseline comparison on an event-grouped, leak-free split, on which a
  classical logistic regression outperforms the fine-tuned model.
keywords:
  - time series
  - anomaly detection
  - satellite telemetry
  - time-series language model
  - spacecraft operations
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-09-13"
